<p>I added new header links at the top of the page to the Homebrew and Archived UA sections. Backgrounds got split into 3 columns which seemed a little cleaner to me.</p>
<p>If you disagree with a specific subclass being moved to the Archived section make your case. It's a subjective thing, but I think that any subclass that was released before the list in Tasha's became semi-official is unlikely to be released in 5e. Or at the least will be re-released in new UA.</p>
<p>Sorry if this seems too semi-official, I'm a developer by trade so that's how I'm used to presenting this stuff to people. I'm not trying to tell everyone how it should be (it's not even my page to do so), but I think all these things make sense.</p>

